ation"}],"definitions":[],"derivation":[],"formalization_refs":[],"mechanism":"Failures appear uncorrelated until a shared cause (e.g., an AWS outage, a shared open-source library vulnerability, or a common training dataset bias) is triggered. Because the shared cause is latent and often external to the operators' control, it is impossible to rule out through observation alone. Thus, independence is a negative claim that cannot be fully verified empirically."
